# neuron-profile capture of every graph the core suite compiled, inf2-a (inf2.xlarge), 2026-09-21.
#
# Run after the pass finished, with nothing else on the device, by
# scripts/throttle_probe.sh: for each NEFF in the compile cache whose mtime
# falls inside the A_core phase window, `neuron-profile capture` then
# `view --output-format summary-json`, filtered to the throttle, cycle,
# tensor-engine and FLOP counters.
#
# Why: inf2 sustained 0.723 of trn1's dense-GEMM rate at identical code and
# toolchain with identical memory bandwidth, and neuron-monitor carries no
# throttle counter. The graphs whose Tensor Engine is busy carry a
# utilization-limit throttle active 84-90% of the time; the idle ones carry
# none. See docs/inf2_sustains_less_than_trn1.md.
#
# Cycle counts here are NOT comparable across captures: the same module read
# 83,411,352 cycles on inf2-a and 273,732,448 on inf2-b.

